  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Icf Incorporated L L C has $269M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date across 487 awards, with an average award size of $553K and obligations down 6.4% year over year. The Department of Health and Human Services is the largest buyer, accounting for $125M of obligations so far. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services is the largest NAICS market, with $94.2M obligated in FY2026 to date. Yearly obligations show a multi-year pattern: FY21 was $469M, FY22 was $509M, FY23 was $540M, FY24 was $489M, FY25 was $288M, and FY26 is $269M to date. Computer Systems Design Services and Custom Computer Programming Services are the second and third markets by obligation, with $56M and $31.9M respectively. Other notable agencies include the Department of Homeland Security at $37.7M and the Environmental Protection Agency at $22.9M. These figures are partial for the current fiscal year and reflect obligations rather than total contract ceilings or award values unless otherwise noted.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations changed over time?",
        "body": "Icf Incorporated L L C obligations peaked at $540M in FY23 and then declined to $489M in FY24 and $288M in FY25. FY26 obligations are $269M to date, which represents a year-over-year change down 6.4%. The multi-year series runs: FY21 $469M, FY22 $509M, FY23 $540M, FY24 $489M, FY25 $288M, FY26 $269M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is Icf Incorporated L L C winning work in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Icf Incorporated L L C is winning the most work from the Department of Health and Human Services at $125M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $37.7M and the Environmental Protection Agency at $22.9M. The largest markets are Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $94.2M and Computer Systems Design Services at $56M. Other sizable markets include Custom Computer Programming Services at $31.9M and Other Computer Related Services at $27.8M."
      }
    ]
  },
